{"id":"01","title":"Greetings","goal":"会話を始め、短い近況の質問に答え、しばらく会っていなかった人と再会したときにあいさつできます。","language":"ja","study":[{"id":"01-study-0","title":"この章のはじめに","blocks":[{"id":"ja-01-study-0-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"まずは、あいさつを一つ、近況を尋ねる言い方を一つ選びます。違う気持ちや場面を表したいときに、選択肢を増やします。この章は文字を見ながら声に出す練習です。音声は付いていません。"}],"span":[4,4],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":4},{"id":"01-study-1","title":"会話を始める","blocks":[{"id":"ja-01-study-1-0","type":"table","header":[[{"text":"英語表現"}],[{"text":"意味と使う場面"}]],"rows":[[[{"text":"Hi.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"相手に声をかけ、やり取りを始める短いあいさつです。「こんにちは」「やあ」などに当たります。"}]],[[{"text":"Hello.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"あいさつです。改まった出会いにも使えますが、改まった場面だけの表現ではありません。"}]],[[{"text":"Hey.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"くだけたあいさつです。この章では、知っている相手に使う例から始めます。"}]],[[{"text":"Good morning.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"朝のあいさつで、「おはようございます」に当たります。"}]]],"span":[8,13],"phraseIds":["ch01-p112829969009517","ch01-p173614268651625","ch01-p68540367868254","ch01-p73116116828724"],"phraseCells":[["ch01-p112829969009517",null],["ch01-p173614268651625",null],["ch01-p68540367868254",null],["ch01-p73116116828724",null]]},{"id":"ja-01-study-1-1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"職場で、よく知っている同僚に会う場面","emphasis":true}],"span":[15,15],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch01-b3","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Good morning."}],"id":"ch01-line17","person":"Alex","en":"Good morning.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"},{"speaker":"Casey","runs":[{"text":"Morning."}],"id":"ch01-line18","person":"Casey","en":"Morning.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg"}],"span":[17,18],"art":"ch01-scene-0.svg","theme":"greeting","people":["Alex","Casey"],"caption":"会話を始める","phraseIds":["ch01-line17","ch01-line18"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-1-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Morning","emphasis":true},{"text":" は朝のあいさつを短くした形です。Caseyは同じ朝のあいさつを返しています。省略せず "},{"text":"Good morning","emphasis":true},{"text":" と返してもかまいません。午後なら "},{"text":"Good afternoon","emphasis":true},{"text":"、夕方や夜に会うなら "},{"text":"Good evening","emphasis":true},{"text":" が使えます。集団に向ける場合は "},{"text":"Hi, everyone","emphasis":true},{"text":"、"},{"text":"Good evening, everyone","emphasis":true},{"text":" という言い方があります。集団へのあいさつの練習は任意です。"}],"span":[20,20],"phraseIds":["ch01-p46968074376467","ch01-p124479204518791","ch01-p134933134068110","ch01-p18508980499428","ch01-p249717618192941","ch01-p43578530053573"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-1-4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"相手との関係、場面、伝えたい気持ちを考えて選びます。職場という理由だけで、あいさつが一つに決まるわけではありません。"},{"text":"Hey","emphasis":true},{"text":" は注意を引く呼びかけにもなるため、その後の言葉や言い方で意味が変わります。"},{"text":"Good night","emphasis":true},{"text":" は通常、別れるときや寝る前のあいさつです。別れの表現は第10章で詳しく扱います。"}],"span":[22,22],"phraseIds":["ch01-p257046360659719","ch01-p242717278344594"]}],"line":6},{"id":"01-study-2","title":"近況を尋ね、答える","blocks":[{"id":"ja-01-study-2-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"How are you?","emphasis":true},{"text":"、"},{"text":"How are you doing?","emphasis":true},{"text":"、"},{"text":"How's it going?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、「調子はどうですか」と短く声をかける表現にも、相手の状況を本当に知りたい質問にもなります。その後の会話が、どちらの意図なのかを判断する手掛かりになります。"}],"span":[26,26],"phraseIds":["ch01-p47926491872939","ch01-p58047280762290","ch01-p243413609921951","ch01-p56938221987892"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-2-1","type":"table","header":[[{"text":"返答"}],[{"text":"伝えられること"}]],"rows":[[[{"text":"Good, thanks.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"「元気です、ありがとう」という短い肯定的な返答です。"}]],[[{"text":"Pretty good.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"「けっこういいです」「かなり順調です」という意味です。"}]],[[{"text":"Not bad.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"「悪くないです」という返答です。言い方によって、肯定的な気持ちや、まずまず満足している気持ちを伝えます。"}]],[[{"text":"I'm okay.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"「大丈夫です」「何とかやっています」などを伝えます。相手を安心させる場合もあります。状況によって意味合いが変わります。"}]],[[{"text":"Not great.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"「あまりよくありません」という返答です。物事が特にうまくいっていないことを伝えます。"}]]],"span":[28,34],"phraseIds":["ch01-p60747133036739","ch01-p33613601583977","ch01-p232249756058560","ch01-p177722320959036","ch01-p96808181408781"],"phraseCells":[["ch01-p60747133036739",null],["ch01-p33613601583977",null],["ch01-p232249756058560",null],["ch01-p177722320959036",null],["ch01-p96808181408781",null]]},{"id":"ja-01-study-2-2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"この表を、気分を上から下まで並べた固定の尺度として覚えないでください。"},{"text":"Fine, thanks","emphasis":true},{"text":" も使える返答です。"},{"text":"How about you?","emphasis":true},{"text":" を加えると、「あなたはどうですか」と相手に質問を返せます。短く、何を尋ねているか明らかなやり取りでは、"},{"text":"You?","emphasis":true},{"text":" も同じ役割を果たします。"}],"span":[36,36],"phraseIds":["ch01-p90719763201242","ch01-p70753857207019"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-2-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"顔見知りどうしの会話","emphasis":true}],"span":[38,38],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch01-b10","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Hey. How's it going?"}],"id":"ch01-line40","person":"Alex","en":"Hey. How's it going?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"},{"speaker":"Casey","runs":[{"text":"Pretty good. You?"}],"id":"ch01-line41","person":"Casey","en":"Pretty good. You?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg"},{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Not bad."}],"id":"ch01-line42","person":"Alex","en":"Not bad.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"}],"span":[40,42],"art":"ch01-scene-1.svg","theme":"greeting","people":["Alex","Casey"],"caption":"近況を尋ね、答える","phraseIds":["ch01-line40","ch01-line41","ch01-line42"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-2-5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Alexが近況を尋ね、Caseyが「けっこういい」と答えて質問を返しています。Alexの返答は「悪くない」です。"}],"span":[44,44],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-01-study-2-6","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"別の返答をする会話","emphasis":true}],"span":[46,46],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch01-b12","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Hello. How are you?"}],"id":"ch01-line46","person":"Alex","en":"Hello. How are you?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"},{"speaker":"Casey","runs":[{"text":"Good, thanks. How about you?"}],"id":"ch01-line47","person":"Casey","en":"Good, thanks. How about you?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg"},{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"I'm okay."}],"id":"ch01-line48","person":"Alex","en":"I'm okay.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"}],"span":[46,48],"art":"ch01-scene-2.svg","theme":"greeting","people":["Alex","Casey"],"caption":"近況を尋ね、答える","phraseIds":["ch01-line46","ch01-line47","ch01-line48"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-2-8","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Caseyは短く肯定的に答えています。Alexは「大丈夫です」など、自分の状態を伝えています。この一言だけから、Alexの気分を細かく決めつけることはできません。"}],"span":[52,52],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-01-study-2-9","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"いつも順調だと言う必要はありません。"},{"text":"Not great","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、あまりよくない状態を正直に伝える選択肢です。相手が立ち止まって時間を取ってくれれば、詳しく話す流れになることもあります。個人的なことを話さず、短く答えて終えてもかまいません。この章では、相談の会話全体ではなく、短い返答を練習します。"}],"span":[54,54],"phraseIds":["ch01-p28111050108215"]}],"line":24},{"id":"01-study-3","title":"再会する","blocks":[{"id":"ja-01-study-3-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Good to see you","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、相手に会えてうれしい気持ちを伝えます。"},{"text":"It's been a while","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、「しばらくぶりですね」と、会っていなかった時間に触れます。"},{"text":"How have you been?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、前に会ってから今までの様子を尋ねます。ここでは使えるまとまりとして覚えます。使うために現在完了の文法を説明できる必要はありません。"}],"span":[58,58],"phraseIds":["ch01-p280699847663469","ch01-p9593477281164","ch01-p36590936486484"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-3-1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"知り合い二人が再会する場面","emphasis":true}],"span":[60,60],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch01-b16","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Hi! Good to see you."}],"id":"ch01-line58","person":"Alex","en":"Hi! Good to see you.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"},{"speaker":"Casey","runs":[{"text":"You too. It's been a while."}],"id":"ch01-line59","person":"Casey","en":"You too. It's been a while.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg"},{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"How have you been?"}],"id":"ch01-line60","person":"Alex","en":"How have you been?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"},{"speaker":"Casey","runs":[{"text":"I've been okay. How about you?"}],"id":"ch01-line61","person":"Casey","en":"I've been okay. How about you?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg"},{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"I've been good."}],"id":"ch01-line62","person":"Alex","en":"I've been good.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"}],"span":[58,62],"art":"ch01-scene-3.svg","theme":"greeting","people":["Alex","Casey"],"caption":"再会する","phraseIds":["ch01-line58","ch01-line59","ch01-line60","ch01-line61","ch01-line62"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-3-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Caseyの "},{"text":"You too","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「こちらも会えてうれしいです」という返答です。この例の "},{"text":"I've been okay","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、会っていなかった期間について控えめに伝えています。別の状況では、同じ言葉にも違う意味合いが出ます。Alexは、その期間を元気に過ごしたと答えています。"},{"text":"How've you been?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、質問の短縮形です。"}],"span":[68,68],"phraseIds":["ch01-p212178324755631","ch01-p128780669360304"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-3-4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Nice to meet you","emphasis":true},{"text":" は初対面の紹介で使える表現で、第2章で扱います。この章が再会に焦点を当てているからといって、初対面では "},{"text":"Good to see you","emphasis":true},{"text":" が使えないという規則にはなりません。"}],"span":[70,70],"phraseIds":["ch01-p58420818387366"]}],"line":56},{"id":"01-study-4","title":"任意: くだけた選択肢","blocks":[{"id":"ja-01-study-4-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"What's up?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、友人へのあいさつになることがあります。"}],"span":[74,74],"phraseIds":["ch01-p206515420014736"]},{"id":"ch01-b20","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Hey, what's up?"}],"id":"ch01-line72","person":"Alex","en":"Hey, what's up?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"},{"speaker":"Casey","runs":[{"text":"Not much. You?"}],"id":"ch01-line73","person":"Casey","en":"Not much. You?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg"},{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Not much."}],"id":"ch01-line74","person":"Alex","en":"Not much.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"}],"span":[72,74],"art":"ch01-scene-4.svg","theme":"greeting","people":["Alex","Casey"],"caption":"任意: くだけた選択肢","phraseIds":["ch01-line72","ch01-line73","ch01-line74"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-4-2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"この例の "},{"text":"Not much","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、「特に新しいことはないです」という意味です。考えられる返答の一つで、必ずこれを返すわけではありません。"}],"span":[80,80],"phraseIds":["ch01-p12652529133176"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-4-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"What's up?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「何が起きているのですか」「どうしたのですか」という質問にもなります。"}],"span":[82,82],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch01-b22","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Alex","runs":[{"text":"Hey, what's up?"}],"id":"ch01-line78","person":"Alex","en":"Hey, what's up?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8508101.svg"},{"speaker":"Casey","runs":[{"text":"I lost my phone."}],"id":"ch01-line79","person":"Casey","en":"I lost my phone.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg"}],"span":[78,79],"art":"ch01-scene-5.svg","theme":"greeting","people":["Alex","Casey"],"caption":"任意: くだけた選択肢","phraseIds":["ch01-line78","ch01-line79"]},{"id":"ja-01-study-4-5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"二つ目の場面では、実際の困り事を尋ねています。Caseyは電話をなくしたと答えています。この一文は場面を理解するための例で、暗記する必要はありません。"}],"span":[87,87],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-01-study-4-6","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Yo","emphasis":true},{"text":" にもくだけたあいさつの用法があります。その話し方で自分の意図を表せるなら、親しい友人の場面で "},{"text":"Yo — Hey, what's up?","emphasis":true},{"text":" を試せます。どの人、どの場面にも使うべきだという指定ではありません。"}],"span":[89,89],"phraseIds":["ch01-p195988010193235","ch01-p107362473098724"]}],"line":72},{"id":"01-words","title":"言葉と表現","blocks":[{"id":"01-glossary","type":"vocabulary","phraseIds":["ch01-v0","ch01-v1","ch01-v2","ch01-v3"]}]}],"practice":[{"id":"01-practice-0","title":"自分の番で答える","blocks":[{"id":"ja-01-practice-0-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"相手のせりふを読んで、自分の返答を声に出します。一人で練習する場合は、両方の役を演じます。必要なときに学習部分を見て、その後、見本を隠してもう一度試します。"}],"span":[93,93],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch01-b26","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"number":1,"runs":[{"text":"同僚が "},{"text":"Good morning","emphasis":true},{"text":" と言います。朝のあいさつを返してください。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-0","sample":[{"text":""},{"text":"Morning","emphasis":true},{"text":" または "},{"text":"Good morning","emphasis":true},{"text":"。短い形でも、全体の形でも、朝のあいさつを返せます。"}]},{"number":2,"runs":[{"text":"知っている人に近況を尋ねます。相手は "},{"text":"Pretty good. You?","emphasis":true},{"text":" と答えます。自分自身、または設定した役に合う返答をしてください。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-1","sample":[{"text":""},{"text":"Hi. How are you?","emphasis":true},{"text":" に続けて "},{"text":"Good, thanks","emphasis":true},{"text":"、"},{"text":"I'm okay","emphasis":true},{"text":"、または場面に合う別の返答が使えます。"}]},{"number":3,"runs":[{"text":"今回の役は大変な一日を過ごしていて、それを短く伝えたい人です。"},{"text":"How are you?","emphasis":true},{"text":" に答えてください。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-2","sample":[{"text":""},{"text":"Not great","emphasis":true},{"text":"。"},{"text":"I'm okay","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、相手を安心させる返答になることもあります。単に「程度が弱い否定」として扱わないでください。"}]},{"number":4,"runs":[{"text":"しばらく会っていなかった知り合いが "},{"text":"Hi! Good to see you","emphasis":true},{"text":" と言います。気持ちを返し、その期間の近況を尋ねてください。相手は "},{"text":"I've been okay. How about you?","emphasis":true},{"text":" と答えます。会話を続けてください。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-3","sample":[{"text":""},{"text":"You too. How have you been?","emphasis":true},{"text":"。その後は "},{"text":"I've been good","emphasis":true},{"text":" または "},{"text":"I've been okay","emphasis":true},{"text":" などで、自分の近況を答えます。"}]},{"number":5,"runs":[{"text":"午後に初めて接する仕事の相手にあいさつします。次に、親しい同僚にあいさつします。相手との関係に対して、その選択がどう合っているか説明してください。同じあいさつを両方で使ってもかまいません。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-4","sample":[{"text":""},{"text":"Hello / Good afternoon / Hi","emphasis":true},{"text":"。同僚には "},{"text":"Hey / Hi / Good afternoon","emphasis":true},{"text":" などが考えられます。関係と伝えたい雰囲気に合うものを選びます。"}]},{"number":6,"runs":[{"text":"How's it going?","emphasis":true},{"text":" と尋ねると、"},{"text":"Not great","emphasis":true},{"text":" と返ってきます。この返答だけで分かることと、分からないことを説明してください。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-5","sample":[{"text":"物事がうまくいっていないと分かります。理由は示されていません。"}]},{"number":7,"runs":[{"text":"任意: 友人に "},{"text":"Yo","emphasis":true},{"text":" または "},{"text":"Hey, what's up?","emphasis":true},{"text":" であいさつし、意味のつながる返答まで練習してください。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-6","sample":[{"text":""},{"text":"Yo — Hey","emphasis":true},{"text":"、または "},{"text":"Hey, what's up? — Not much. You?","emphasis":true},{"text":"。あいさつや近況の質問に合う返答をつなぎます。"}]},{"number":8,"runs":[{"text":"任意: 夜の集団ミーティングで、最初のあいさつをしてください。"}],"id":"ch01-b26-7","sample":[{"text":""},{"text":"Good evening, everyone","emphasis":true},{"text":" または "},{"text":"Hello, everyone","emphasis":true},{"text":"。集団全体へのあいさつです。"}]}],"span":[95,102],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":91,"answers":[{"id":"ja-01-practice-0-4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"後で、相手との関係や返答を変えて、一つのやり取りを再練習してください。会話を始められるか、自分の状態を伝えられるか、相手の言葉に合う返答ができるかを確認します。一つの声やアクセントをそっくりにまねることだけが目標ではありません。録音を聞いて繰り返す練習やシャドーイングには、実際の音声が必要です。"}],"span":[115,115],"phraseIds":[]}]}],"phrases":[{"id":"ch01-p112829969009517","en":"Hi.","section":"01-study-1","context":"相手に声をかけ、やり取りを始める短いあいさつです。「こんにちは」「やあ」などに当たります。","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch01-p112829969009517"},{"id":"ch01-p173614268651625","en":"Hello.","section":"01-study-1","context":"あいさつです。改まった出会いにも使えますが、改まった場面だけの表現ではありません。","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch01-p173614268651625"},{"id":"ch01-p68540367868254","en":"Hey.","section":"01-study-1","context":"くだけたあいさつです。この章では、知っている相手に使う例から始めます。","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch01-p68540367868254"},{"art":"word-greeting.svg","id":"ch01-p73116116828724","en":"Good morning.","section":"01-study-1","context":"朝のあいさつで、「おはようございます」に当たります。","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch01-p73116116828724"},{"id":"ch01-line18","en":"Morning.","section":"01-study-1","context":"会話を始める","kind":"phrase","speaker":"Casey","portrait":"portrait-265283458.svg","ja":"","studyId":"ch01-line18"},{"id":"ch01-p134933134068110","en":"Good afternoon","section":"01-study-1","context":"会話を始める","kind":"word","ja":"","s